 of solid tumors; and EVX-04, a therapeutic cancer vaccine candidate, which is in phase 1 trial for acute myeloid leukemia. Its programs also include vaccines that are in pre-clinical stage, which includes EVX-B1, a multi-component prophylactic vaccine targeting skin and soft tissue infections with S. aureus bacteria; EVX-B2 to target multi-component prophylactic vaccine against gonorrhea bacteria; EVX-B3 to target bacterial pathogen associated with repeated infections; and EVX-V1, a multi-component prophylactic vaccine candidate for cytomegalovirus. The company was formerly known as Evaxion Biotech A/S and changed its name to Evaxion A/S in May 2025. Evaxion A/S was incorporated in 2008 and is based in Horsholm, Denmark."}}